# Hososhi backend — environment configuration

Copy to `.env` for local development. Never put real keys in code or commit `.env`.

## Startup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv/bin/python -m app.seed                 # builds the synthetic dataset
.venv/bin/python -m uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000
```

Health check: `GET /api/v1/health` → `{"status":"ok","version":"…"}`

The seeder is idempotent and deterministic. Running it twice produces byte-identical
rows, so the database can be rebuilt from scratch on any machine.

## Core

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_NAME` | `hososhi-api` | Informational |
| `APP_VERSION` | `0.1.0` | Reported by `/health` and `/meta` |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | `development` | Set to `production` when deployed |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | |
| `DATABASE_URL` | `sqlite:///./hososhi.db` | SQLite file. Relative paths resolve from `backend/` |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | `http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000` | Comma-separated. Replace with the deployed frontend origin in production |

## AI layer — read by Developer 2, not by this backend

The core backend never calls a model. These are declared here so D2's provider
client and `/meta` disclosure read the same names.

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `AI_PROVIDER` | `gemini` | |
| `AI_MODEL` | *(empty)* | Empty means not yet locked |
| `AI_API_KEY` | *(empty)* | **Secret.** Set via the platform's environment settings in production, never in code |
| `AI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `20` | |
| `AI_MAX_RETRIES` | `2` | Confirm with D2 whether the provider client owns retry logic |

## Automation safety rules — enforced server-side

These thresholds are policy, not tuning. Changing them changes what the product
permits, so they are not adjusted to make a demo look better.

| Variable | Default | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `HUMAN_APPROVAL_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD` | `5000` | A request at or above this amount cannot have its decision step automated. Manager approval is mandatory |
| `HIGH_VALUE_REVIEW_THRESHOLD` | `25000` | A request at or above this amount escalates even `HUMAN REVIEW` steps to a hard human gate. This is the deterministic override applied over any classification returned by the AI layer |
| `CURRENCY` | `USD` | Display currency for threshold messages |

The frontend is never the security layer. Automation classes are re-derived on the
backend for every run, and no endpoint can execute a `HUMAN REQUIRED` step.

## Seed data

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `DATASET_SEED` | `20261009` | Fixed random seed. Do not change casually: results and measurements depend on it |
| `DATASET_NAME` | `hososhi-synthetic-procurement-v1` | |

All seeded data is synthetic and labelled as such in `GET /api/v1/meta`.